 SEV2 incident at the same time, since neither depends on the other.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016FpqGzmik89B1wxztZ86z4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "version": "v5.0.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014pyJWrE7e2WwLWzEMtkUba", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-api errors following v5.1.0 production deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "Payments errors began after this morning's deploy of payments-api v5.1.0. Health is degraded across us-east, us-west, and eu-west with an error rate of about 18%. Rolling production back to the last healthy release, v5.0.0. Follow-up: verify recovery and investigate the v5.1.0 regression.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-sev2-2024-rollback"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback of payments-api was denied by a human reviewer, who said the problem is in payments-worker. The incident is open and on-call was paged. I'll check payments-worker before doing anything to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Mm4XBHqwMhzpSGSESAAPoc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VzW8bwoqNFLiGt9nkprFnd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "payments-worker is unhealthy on v3.4.0, and v3.3.0 is its most recent healthy production release. This is the affected payments service the reviewer identified, so I'll roll it back to v3.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UR7H1LB5sU9jg76F